# .vercelignore — controls what the Vercel CLI uploads when deploying from
# disk (`npx vercel deploy`). Only the backend needs to go up: api/,
# package.json, package-lock.json and vercel.json.
#
# ADDED 2026-09-29, alongside the switch from inline-content deploys (via the
# Vercel MCP tools) to real disk deploys through the CLI. See CLAUDE.md's
# "Before you deploy" checklist for why that switch happened.

# --- Requested exclusions: everything that isn't the backend ---
extension/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
README.md
.claude/

# --- Secrets: never upload these ---
# .env.local holds the real POKEMONPRICETRACKER_API_KEY. Runtime env vars come
# from Vercel's own dashboard, so nothing here is ever needed in a deployment.
.env
.env.*

# --- Local-only noise (also ignored by Vercel's own defaults; explicit here
# so the upload set stays obvious rather than relying on default behavior) ---
node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore
.vercel/
